title: OutcastKinMotileIntro
---
Outcast Kin: Greetings. I had hoped you'd find your way here. Please make yourself comfortable.
Outcast Kin: So long as you are peaceful while here, you may rest here as long as you like.
-> I thank you, kind being. I have some questions.
    <<jump QuestionsForTheOutcastMotile>>
-> I have to go. I'll be seeing you.
===

title: QuestionsForTheOutcastMotile
---
-> What can I call you?
    Outcast Kin: I am but a namless exiled motile, cut off from the Kin. You may call me Salah if you wish. I find you humans need to give names,
    Outcast Kin: to everything and everyone. A product of your auditory communication, perhaps? We communicate more directly, and need not.
-> Ask about the surrounding area
    Outcast Kin: To the north is the true no man's land. Not much reason to go there, except that beyond it is edge of Kin territory.
    Outcast Kin: To the south is human controlled territory, as you may know. For one such as me, and I suspect for you, is sealed.
    <<jump QuestionsForTheOutcastMotile>>
-> What is the Kin? My memories are still coming back in bits and pieces.
    Outcast Kin: Not to worry. Kin is the threefold Triarchy of species which has dominated this world for untold millenia.
    Outcast Kin: I am but a stray motile, cut off from the Kinship. Motiles, Keepers, and Cores, three species, one past, one destiny.
    <<jump AskAboutSpecificKinSpecies>>
-> What kind of store is this?
    Outcast Kin: It is whatever it needs to be. I confess I rarely have need to trade and do business. I find the idea quite invigorating!
    Outcast Kin: In the old days, before the great Burrowing, we Motiles were quite the merchants. We'd trade goods between pods of Kin, spread across the surface.
    Outcast Kin: Can you just imagine? Alas, I have some setting up to do still.
-> [Leave]
===

title: AskAboutSpecificKinSpecies
---
-> Ask about the Motiles
    Outcast Kin: Each has a role to play. Motiles such as I are defined by our mobility, and not our intellect.
    <<jump AskAboutSpecificKinSpecies>>
-> Ask about the Keepers
    Outcast Kin: Keepers are our nurturers, and they are natural mediators. They tend to stay in one place.
    <<jump AskAboutSpecificKinSpecies>>
-> Ask about the Cores
    Outcast Kin: Cores are our thinkers, our scientists, and philosophers, and kings. They are the most misunderstood by humans.
    Outcast Kin: Human exploitation of the Cores is what drove us to war. I believe they may not have known what they did. Alas,
    Outcast Kin: ichor has been spilled on both sides.
    <<jump AskAboutSpecificKinSpecies>>
-> Actually I had a different questions
    <<jump QuestionsForTheOutcastMotile>>
-> [Leave]
===